  "notes": "Loop-pedal singer-songwriter pop with grime and dancehall rhythmic borrowings, and the one model in this batch whose backbeat is displaced rather than plain: the research says 2&4 straight \"but frequently displaced by a tresillo (3+3+2) accent pattern rather than a plain backbeat\", so `hihat.base` is weighted toward the literal `tresillo` value and `kick.tresilloBias` is the highest number in this file at 0.62. The percussion lanes come from the documented device — \"percussion generated from the guitar body — he taps the guitar and layers it into the track — plus programmed kick, clap and a marimba/keyboard hit doubling as percussion\" — which is `perc`, `rim` and `woodblock` at a high density with the snare stack reduced to a clap. \"Loop-pedal construction means patterns are built as stacked 1- or 2-bar layers that never change length\", so the fills are pushed out to 8 and 16 bars and the roll ladder is off. Harmony is stated outright: \"four-chord minor loops, most characteristically i—iv—VI—VII\", carrying top weight; \"capo'd small-bodied Martin guitars give close, high triad voicings\" is `voicing.style` close with a high `triad` share and a raised register. Melody register is the documented G♯3—G♯5 tenor span \"written to sit right at the top of the chest voice for hooks\"; \"syllable-dense and rap-adjacent in verses … then open into long sustained chorus notes\" is the wide `densityPerBar` and `endVariation`, and \"melodic motion is stepwise with a repeated pivot note\" is the 0.8 step share and the small `motifPitchCount`. No `bass808` block: the entry describes sub-bass and simple synth bass on roots, and in the looped form no bass at all. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are every drum probability, the humanize pair and `bpm.mode` 88 (the research gives 76—100 ballad core and 90—100 percussive-pop, so the mode is the midpoint of the first-named band).",
